@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    ManageGames keeps all data in its own PostgreSQL database, run by whoever hosts this installation.
    There is no analytics or tracking.
</p>
<p>
    To find cover pictures, the server sends the titles of your games, and nothing else, to the cover sources
    this installation is set up with: <a href="https://www.screenscraper.fr">ScreenScraper</a>,
    <a href="https://www.igdb.com">IGDB</a> (run by Twitch) and <a href="https://www.steamgriddb.com">SteamGridDB</a>. Their pictures are downloaded by the server and
    stored with your games; your browser never contacts these sites. Uploaded pictures stay on this server.
</p>
<p>The app only sets the cookies it needs to work:</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>__Host-ManageGames.Auth</code> keeps you signed in on this device. It ends when you log out, usually when you close the browser, after two hours without activity and at the latest after twelve hours.</li>
    <li><code>__Host-ManageGames.Antiforgery</code> protects the forms against cross-site request forgery.</li>
    <li><code>__Host-ManageGames.TempData</code> carries one-time notices, such as a failed login, to the next page.</li>
</ul>
<p>Passwords are stored only as salted hashes (PBKDF2).</p>
